@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceParticipant {
  BorderColor #16A34A
  BackgroundColor #DCFCE7
}
skinparam participant<<model>> {
  BorderColor #2563EB
  BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
}
skinparam participant<<ext>> {
  BorderColor #7C3AED
  BackgroundColor #EDE9FE
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #6B7280
  BackgroundColor #F3F4F6
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}

title Durable execution: journal, crash, resume

participant "Agent loop\n(workflow code)" as W
database "Journal" as J
participant "LLM" as M <<model>>
participant "Payment API\n(external)" as P <<ext>>

== First run ==
W -> M : step 1: model call
M --> W : tool request (charge)
W -> J : persist model result
note right of J
  Replay will reuse this result,
  so the call is not re-billed
end note

W -> P : step 2: charge\n(Idempotency-Key = step ID)
P -> P : performs the charge
P --> W : result
note over W, P #FEE2E2
  **Crash** after the external action
  but before the result is persisted
end note

== Resume from journal ==
W -> J : load journal
J --> W : step 1 recorded, step 2 absent
W -> W : step 1 skipped (result replayed)
W -> P : step 2 retried\n(same Idempotency-Key)
P --> W : repeat treated as one action\n(no second charge)
W -> J : persist step 2 result

note over W, P
  Journal prevents re-running completed steps.
  Idempotency keys make the in-flight step safe.
  Separate runs need a business ID or a DB uniqueness constraint.
end note
@enduml
